# 💾 System Images for Bumblebee

This folder contains Raspberry Pi system images for the Bumblebee drone.

Flash the image to an SD card and insert it into the drone's Raspberry Pi — no additional setup required. The image ships Ubuntu 24.04 with ROS 2 Jazzy and the full pre-built Bumblebee stack (login `lb` / `lb`).

Available images and download links: see [download.md](download.md).

For full flashing instructions and first-boot steps:
👉 **[SD Card Image — Bumblebee Students Wiki](https://github.com/futureLabKezad/bumblebee-students/wiki/SD‐Card‐Image)**

## Flashing the Image

```bash
# Flash straight from the .img.gz (replace /dev/sdX with your SD card)
gunzip -c bumblebee.img.gz | sudo dd of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress
```

Or use **[Raspberry Pi Imager](https://www.raspberrypi.com/software/)** for a simpler experience — it accepts the `.img.gz` directly, no need to unpack.
